# What must never reach a build context.
#
# The Dockerfile copies named paths rather than `COPY . .`, so this is a second
# line of defence — but it is the line that matters, because the two worst
# things in a developer's checkout are patient data and a local config, and both
# are .gitignore'd (invisible to git, fully visible to docker build).

# Real studies. A developer machine that has run the app has DICOM in these.
#
# Two layouts, and both need naming. The root-anchored paths are the desktop
# layout (~/CarinoPACS or a checkout that has been run in place). /data/ is the
# layout docker-compose.yml itself tells operators to create — and a pattern
# anchored at the root never matches below it, so without this entry the whole
# of ./data ships to the daemon and sits in its build cache.
/received/
/outgoing/
/sent/
/pending/
/ris/
/logs/
/index.db
/data/
*.dcm

# Machine-specific config: AE titles, destination hosts, and the dashboard
# token. The file the image ships is config.example.json.
/config.json
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

# The two places compose puts the dashboard token. .env is read by compose
# itself, so it exists on exactly the machines that build this image.
/secrets/
.env

# The app writes atomically — new content to `<name>.tmp.<pid>`, then rename.
# A file that vanishes mid-COPY fails the build outright, so exclude the
# window rather than lose builds to a race with a running instance.
*.tmp
*.tmp.*

# Host virtualenv. Its interpreter is a copied symlink that does not work
# anywhere else, and it would be the largest thing in the image.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Host-architecture bytecode would shadow the container's.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Electron desktop shell and installer output — nothing to do with the server.
desktop/
/build/
/dist/
*.AppImage
*.exe
*.dmg

# Host wrappers that assume a local venv; misleading inside a container.
run.sh
run.ps1
setup.sh
setup.ps1
reset.sh
test_print.py

# Repo furniture
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.claude/
docs/
# ...except the manual, which the image serves at /manual/ so a container on an
# isolated clinical network still has its documentation. The two lines are not
# redundant: the first re-admits the directory, the second its contents, and
# with only one of them the COPY below fails on an empty or missing path.
!docs/manual
!docs/manual/**
# ...but not the harness that REGENERATES the figures. A screenshot driver, a
# DICOM forger and a traffic seeder are not documentation an operator reads,
# and a traffic generator inside a medical appliance image is a thing somebody
# has to explain in a review. Last match wins, so this comes after the two
# lines above. packaging/pacs-engine.spec holds the same name back.
docs/manual/tools
docs/manual/tools/**
tests/
BUILDING.md
CHANGELOG.md
README.md
docker-compose*.yml
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
